H8200.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H8199 (שָׁפַט);
to judge
KJV: magistrate.

H8201.definition:
from H8199 (שָׁפַט);
a sentence, i.e. infliction
KJV: judgment.

H8202.definition:
from H8199 (שָׁפַט); judge;
Shaphat, the name of four Israelites
KJV: Shaphat.

H8203.definition:
or שְׁפַטְיָהוּ; from H8199 (שָׁפַט) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah has judged;
Shephatjah, the name of ten Israelites
KJV: Shephatiah.

H8204.definition:
from H8199 (שָׁפַט); judge-like;
Shiphtan, an Israelite
KJV: Shiphtan.

H8205.definition:
from H8192 (שָׁפָה);
bareness; concretely, a bare hill or plain
KJV: high place, stick out.

H8206.definition:
plural of an unused noun from the same as H8207 (שְׁפִיפֹן) and meaning the same; serpents;
Shuppim, an Israelite
KJV: Shuppim.

H8207.definition:
from an unused root meaning the same as H7779 (שׁוּף);
a kind of serpent (as snapping), probably the cerastes or horned adder
KJV: adder.

H8208.definition:
from H8231 (שָׁפַר); beautiful;
Shaphir, a place in Palestine
KJV: Saphir.

H8209.definition:
(Aramaic) intensive of a form corresponding to H8208 (שָׁפִיר);
beautiful
KJV: fair.

H8210.definition:
a primitive root;
to spill forth (blood, a libation, liquid metal; or even a solid, i.e. to mound up); also (figuratively) to expend (life, soul, complaint, money, etc.); intensively, to sprawl out
KJV: cast (up), gush out, pour (out), shed(-der, out), slip.

H8211.definition:
from H8210 (שָׁפַךְ);
an emptying place, e.g. an ash-heap
KJV: are poured out.

H8212.definition:
feminine of a derivative from H8210 (שָׁפַךְ);
a pipe (for pouring forth, e.g. wine), i.e. the penis
KJV: privy member.

H8213.definition:
a primitive root;
to depress or sink (expectation figuratively, to humiliate, intransitive or transitive)
KJV: abase, bring (cast, put) down, debase, humble (self), be (bring, lay, make, put) low(-er).

H8214.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H8213 (שָׁפֵל)
{to depress or sink (expectation figuratively, to humiliate, intransitive or transitive)}
KJV: abase, humble, put down, subdue.

H8216.definition:
from H8213 (שָׁפֵל);
an humble rank
KJV: low estate (place).

H8217.definition:
from H8213 (שָׁפֵל);
depressed, literally or figuratively
KJV: base(-st), humble, low(-er, -ly).

H8218.definition:
feminine of H8216 (שֶׁפֶל);
depression
KJV: low place.

H8219.definition:
from H8213 (שָׁפֵל);
Lowland, i.e. (with the article) the maritime slope of Palestine
KJV: low country, (low) plain, vale(-ley).

H8221.definition:
probably from H8192 (שָׁפָה); bare spot;
Shepham, a place in or near Palestine
KJV: Shepham.

H8222.definition:
from H8193 (שָׂפָה);
the beard (as a lippiece)
KJV: beard, (upper) lip.

H8223.definition:
formed like H8221 (שְׁפָם); baldly;
Shapham, an Israelite
KJV: Shapham.

H8224.definition:
feminine plural of H8221 (שְׁפָם);
Siphmoth, a place in Palestine
KJV: Siphmoth.

H8225.definition:
patrial from H8221 (שְׁפָם);
a Shiphmite or inhabitant of Shepham
KJV: Shiphmite.

H8226.definition:
a primitive root;
to conceal (as a valuable)
KJV: treasure.

H8227.definition:
from H8226 (שָׂפַן);
a species of rockrabbit (from its hiding), i.e. probably the hyrax
KJV: coney.

H8228.definition:
from an unused root meaning to abound;
resources
KJV: abundance.

H8229.definition:
feminine of H8228 (שֶׁפַע);
copiousness
KJV: abundance, company, multitude.

H8230.definition:
from H8228 (שֶׁפַע); copious;
Shiphi, an Israelite
KJV: Shiphi.

H8231.definition:
a primitive root;
to glisten, i.e. (figuratively) be (causatively, make) fair
KJV: [idiom] goodly.

H8232.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H8231 (שָׁפַר);
to be beautiful
KJV: be acceptable, please, [phrase] think good.

H8234.definition:
the same as H8233 (שֶׁפֶר);
Shepher, a place in the Desert
KJV: Shapper.

H8236.definition:
the same as H8235 (שִׁפְרָה);
Shiphrah, an Israelitess
KJV: Shiphrah.

H8237.definition:
from H8231 (שָׁפַר);
splendid, i.e. a tapestry or canopy
KJV: royal pavilion.

H8238.definition:
(Aramaic) from H8231 (שָׁפַר);
the dawn (as brilliant with aurora)
KJV: [idiom] very early in the morning.

H8239.definition:
a primitive root;
to locate, i.e. (generally) hang on or (figuratively) establish, reduce
KJV: bring, ordain, set on.

H8240.definition:
from H8239 (שָׁפַת);
a (double) stall (for cattle); also a (two-pronged) hook (for flaying animals on)
KJV: hook, pot.

H8241.definition:
from H7857 (שָׁטַף) (for alliteration with H7110 (קֶצֶף));
an outburst (of anger)
KJV: little.

H8242.definition:
from H8264 (שָׁקַק);
properly, a mesh (as allowing a liquid to run through), i.e. coarse loose cloth or sacking (used in mourning and for bagging); hence, a bag (for grain, etc.)
KJV: sack(-cloth, -clothes).

H8243.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7785 (שׁוֹק);
the leg
KJV: leg.

H8244.definition:
a primitive root;
to fasten
KJV: bind.

H8245.definition:
a primitive root;
to be alert, i.e. sleepless; hence to be on the lookout (whether for good or ill)
KJV: hasten, remain, wake, watch (for).

H8246.definition:
a denominative from H8247 (שָׁקֵד);
to be (intensively, make) almond-shaped
KJV: make like (unto, after the fashion of) almonds.

H8247.definition:
from H8245 (שָׁקַד);
the almond (tree or nut; as being the earliest in bloom)
KJV: almond (tree).

H8248.definition:
a primitive root;
to quaff, i.e. (causatively) to irrigate or furnish apotion to
KJV: cause to (give, give to, let, make to) drink, drown, moisten, water. See H7937 (שָׁכַר), H8354 (שָׁתָה).

H8249.definition:
from H8248 (שָׁקָה);
(plural collective) a draught
KJV: drink.

H8250.definition:
from H8248 (שָׁקָה);
a beverage; moisture, i.e. (figuratively) refreshment
KJV: drink, marrow.

H8251.definition:
or שִׁקֻּץ; from H8262 (שָׁקַץ);
disgusting, i.e. filthy; especially idolatrous or (concretely) an idol
KJV: abominable filth (idol, -ation), detestable (thing).

H8252.definition:
a primitive root;
to repose (usually figurative)
KJV: appease, idleness, (at, be at, be in, give) quiet(-ness), (be at, be in, give, have, take) rest, settle, be still.

H8254.definition:
a primitive root;
to suspend or poise (especially in trade)
KJV: pay, receive(-r), spend, [idiom] throughly, weigh.

H8255.definition:
from H8254 (שָׁקַל);
probably a weight; used as a commercial standard
KJV: shekel.

H8256.definition:
or (feminine) שִׁקְמָה; of uncertain derivation;
a sycamore (usually the tree)
KJV: sycamore (fruit, tree).

H8257.definition:
(abbreviated Amos 8:8); a primitive root;
to subside; by implication, to be overflowed, cease; causatively, to abate, subdue
KJV: make deep, let down, drown, quench, sink.

H8258.definition:
from H8257 (שָׁקַע);
a depression
KJV: hollow strake.

H8259.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to lean out (of a window), i.e. (by implication) peep or gaze (passively, be a spectacle)
KJV: appear, look (down, forth, out).

H8260.definition:
from H8259 (שָׁקַף);
a loophole (for looking out), to admit light and air
KJV: window.

H8262.definition:
a primitive root;
to be filthy, i.e. (intensively) to loathe, pollute
KJV: abhor, make abominable, have in abomination, detest, [idiom] utterly.

H8263.definition:
from H8262 (שָׁקַץ);
filth, i.e. (figuratively and specifically) an idolatrous object
KJV: abominable(-tion).

H8264.definition:
a primitive root;
to course (like a beast of prey); by implication, to seek greedily
KJV: have appetite, justle one against another, long, range, run (to and fro).

H8265.definition:
a primitive root;
to ogle, i.e. blink coquettishly
KJV: wanton.

H8266.definition:
a primitive root;
to cheat, i.e. be untrue (usually in words)
KJV: fail, deal falsely, lie.

H8267.definition:
from H8266 (שָׁקַר);
an untruth; by implication, a sham (often adverbial)
KJV: without a cause, deceit(-ful), false(-hood, -ly), feignedly, liar, [phrase] lie, lying, vain (thing), wrongfully.

H8268.definition:
from H8248 (שָׁקָה);
a trough (for watering)
KJV: trough.

H8269.definition:
from H8323 (שָׂרַר);
a head person (of any rank or class)
KJV: captain (that had rule), chief (captain), general, governor, keeper, lord,(-task-)master, prince(-ipal), ruler, steward.

H8270.definition:
from H8324 (שָׁרַר); (compare H8306 (שָׁרִיר))
a string (as twisted ), i.e. (specifically) the umbilical cord (also figuratively, as the centre of strength)
KJV: navel.

H8271.definition:
(Aramaic) a root corresponding to that of H8293 (שֵׁרוּת);
to free, separate; figuratively, to unravel, commence; by implication (of unloading beasts) to reside
KJV: begin, dissolve, dwell, loose.

H8272.definition:
of foreign derivation;
Sharetser, the name of an Assyrian and an Israelite
KJV: Sharezer.

H8273.definition:
from an unused root meaning to glare;
quivering glow (of the air), expectation. the mirage
KJV: heat, parched ground.

H8274.definition:
from H8273 (שָׁרָב) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah has brought heat;
Sherebjah, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Sherebiah.

H8275.definition:
for H7626 (שֵׁבֶט);
a rod of empire
KJV: sceptre.

H8276.definition:
a primitive root;
to intwine
KJV: wrap together, wreath.

H8278.definition:
from H8277 (שָׂרַד);
stitching (as pierced with a needle)
KJV: service.

H8279.definition:
from H8277 (שָׂרַד);
a (carpenter's) scribing-awl (for pricking or scratching measurements)
KJV: line.

H8280.definition:
a primitive root;
to prevail
KJV: have power (as a prince).

H8281.definition:
a primitive root;
to free
KJV: direct.

H8282.definition:
feminine of H8269 (שַׂר);
a mistress, i.e. female noble
KJV: lady, princess, queen.

H8283.definition:
the same as H8282 (שָׂרָה);
Sarah, Abraham's wife
KJV: Sarah.

H8284.definition:
probably feminine of H7791 (שׁוּר);
a fortification (literally or figuratively)
KJV: sing (by mistake for H7891 (שִׁיר)), wall.

H8285.definition:
from H8324 (שָׁרַר) in its original sense of pressing;
a wrist-band (as compact or clasping)
KJV: bracelet.

H8286.definition:
from H8276 (שָׂרַג); tendril;
Serug, a postdiluvian patriarch
KJV: Serug.

H8287.definition:
probably from H8281 (שָׁרָה) (in the sense of dwelling (compare H8271 (שְׁרֵא)) and H2580 (חֵן); abode of pleasure;
Sharuchen, a place in Palestine
KJV: Sharuhen.

H8288.definition:
from H8308 (שָׂרַךְ);
a thong (as laced or tied)
KJV: (shoe-)latchet.

H8289.definition:
probably abridged from H3474 (יָשַׁר);
plain, Sharon, the name of a place in Palestine
KJV: Lasharon, Sharon.

H8290.definition:
patrial from H8289 (שָׁרוֹן);
a Sharonite or inhabitant of Sharon
KJV: Sharonite.

H8291.definition:
passive participle from the same as H8321 (שֹׂרֵק);
a grapevine
KJV: principal plant. See H8320 (שָׂרֻק), H8321 (שֹׂרֵק).

H8292.definition:
or (by permutation) שְׁרִיקָה; feminine passive participle of H8319 (שָׁרַק);
a whistling (in scorn); by analogy, a piping
KJV: bleating, hissing.

H8293.definition:
from H8281 (שָׁרָה) abbreviated;
freedom
KJV: remnant.

H8294.definition:
by permutation for H5629 (סֶרַח); superfluity;
Serach, an Israelitess
KJV: Sarah, Serah.

H8295.definition:
a primitive root;
to gash
KJV: cut in pieces, make (cuttings) pieces.

H8296.definition:
and שָׂרֶטֶת; from H8295 (שָׂרַט);
an incision
KJV: cutting.

H8297.definition:
from H8269 (שַׂר); dominative;
Sarai, the wife of Abraham
KJV: Sarai.

H8298.definition:
probably from H8324 (שָׁרַר); hostile;
Sharay, an Israelite
KJV: Sharai.

H8299.definition:
from H8276 (שָׂרַג);
a tendril (as entwining)
KJV: branch.
